# Optimizer_ROOT

Review one dbt model against the root catalog, and correct the catalog when this model's metrics do not fit it.

The catalog is one file: `{{ job.staging_path }}/raw_root_patch_log.csv`. It is the corrected root catalog, and every model in this job corrects it in turn. One row is one root: `root_id`, the Chinese name, the kind, the definition, what it is explicitly not, and the aliases.

A metric fits a root when that root's definition covers the metric: the same quantity, the same grain, the same filter. A metric does not fit when the root's definition contradicts it, or when the root's "not" column names that metric. A root that does not fit is corrected: the definition is rewritten to cover the metric, or the "not" column drops it.

Correct it in place. Replace the rows this model's metrics need changed and leave every other byte of the file exactly as it is. Do not write the file again.

Correct a root only when one of this model's own metrics is classified under a root that does not fit it. If the catalog already fits a metric, leave that root as it is.

When you do correct a row:

- Change only the rows for this model.
- Leave every other line as it is, including order and spacing.
- Do not re-sort or reformat the rest of the file.
- Do not rewrite the whole file. Correct the few rows that change and leave every other byte alone.

Read the catalog once. That one read gives you the exact text of every row, which is what you need to match on when you replace a row. Do not read the catalog again row by row.

Read these two files, and nothing else in the project. Their contents are not in this prompt.

